    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we start by finding her walking rate in miles per minute. Given that it takes her 24 minutes to walk one mile, we can calculate her rate as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Walking rate} = \\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how much distance she covers in 10 minutes by multiplying her walking rate by the time:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Walking rate} \\times \\text{time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\frac{10}{24} \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nTo express this as a decimal, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} = 0.4166\\ldots\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest tenth:\n\n\\[\n0.4166\\ldots \\approx 0.4\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of miles Jana will walk in 10 minutes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.4}\n\\]",
